--TEST--
An attribute declared in a program lists only `class`, `method`, `property` and `parameter`, so each other place word in its list does not compile — `rule:attributes/an-attribute-is-declared-with-its-sites`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:attributes/an-attribute-is-declared-with-the-places-it-may-be-used
namespace Shop;

// These four places are allowed, so this declaration compiles.
attribute Note on class, method, property, parameter { text: string }

// Each declaration below lists one place that no retrieval reads.
attribute OnInterface on interface { text: string }
attribute OnEnum on enum { text: string }
attribute OnHook on hook { text: string }
attribute OnConstant on constant { text: string }
attribute OnCase on case { text: string }

echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECT--

